✅ 1. Start MongoDB in Ubuntu

sudo systemctl start mongod

To check the status:

sudo systemctl status mongod

To enable on boot:

sudo systemctl enable mongod

✅ 2. Open Mongo Shell

mongosh

✅ 3. Create or Switch to a Database

use myDatabase

    If the database doesn't exist, MongoDB will create it once you insert data.

✅ 4. Create a Collection

db.createCollection("users")

Or you can let MongoDB create it automatically when inserting the first document.
✅ 5. Insert Data (Create)

db.users.insertOne({
  name: "Alice",
  age: 25,
  city: "Pune"
})

db.users.insertMany([
  { name: "Bob", age: 30, city: "Delhi" },
  { name: "Charlie", age: 22, city: "Mumbai" }
])

✅ 6. Read Data

db.users.find()                             // Read all
db.users.find({ city: "Pune" })            // Filter
db.users.find().limit(2)                   // Limit
db.users.find().sort({ age: 1 })           // Sort Asc
db.users.find().sort({ age: -1 })          // Sort Desc

✅ 7. Update Data

db.users.updateOne(
  { name: "Alice" },
  { $set: { age: 26 } }
)

db.users.updateMany(
  { city: "Pune" },
  { $set: { country: "India" } }
)

✅ 8. Delete Data

db.users.deleteOne({ name: "Charlie" })

db.users.deleteMany({ city: "Delhi" })

✅ 9. Aggregation (Average)

db.users.aggregate([
  {
    $group: {
      _id: null,
      averageAge: { $avg: "$age" }
    }
  }
])

✅ 10. Filter Examples

db.users.find({ age: { $gt: 25 } })                   // Greater than
db.users.find({ city: { $in: ["Pune", "Mumbai"] } })  // In array
db.users.find({ age: { $gte: 20, $lte: 30 } })         // Between

✅ 11. Create a View

db.createView(
  "youngUsers",              // View name
  "users",                   // Source collection
  [ { $match: { age: { $lt: 30 } } } ]   // Pipeline
)

To see the view:

db.youngUsers.find()

✅ 12. List All Databases and Collections

show dbs          // List databases
use myDatabase    // Switch to your DB
show collections  // List collections

✅ 13. Exit Mongo Shell

exit
